        "original_id": "ea916d9c-504d-55f7-a0c1-da06e52b0f38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John J. Pershing\n- Organizations: American Expeditionary Force, United States Army, 3d Pursuit Group, 1st Pursuit Wing\n- Events: Battle of Saint-Mihiel, Meuse-Argonne Offensive, World War I\n- Places: France, Western Front\n\nFacts:\n- John J. Pershing was born on September 13, 1860, and he became a senior United States Army officer.\n- John J. Pershing served as commander of the American Expeditionary Force on the Western Front during World War I from 1917 to 1918.\n- The 3d Pursuit Group was formed in France in July 1918 and was assigned to the 1st Pursuit Wing.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel was fought from 12 to 15 September 1918 as a major World War I battle.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel involved the American Expeditionary Force and 110,000 French troops under General John J. Pershing against German positions.\n- The 3d Pursuit Group saw action in the final months of World War I in support of the Battle of Saint-Mihiel and the Meuse-Argonne Offensive.\n- John J. Pershing died on July 15, 1948.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cb9a09f9-d6ae-5b2b-8547-143168af757f",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Saint-Mihiel. Sentence: The Battle of Saint-Mihiel was a major World War I battle fought from 12–15 September 1918, involving the American Expeditionary Force (AEF) and 110,000 French troops under the command of General John J. Pershing of the United States against German positions.\nPage: John J. Pershing. Sentence: General of the Armies John Joseph \"Black Jack\" Pershing (September 13, 1860 – July 15, 1948) was a senior United States Army officer.\nPage: John J. Pershing. Sentence: His most famous post was when he served as the commander of the American Expeditionary Force (AEF) on the Western Front in World War I, 1917–18.\nPage: 3d Pursuit Group. Sentence: Formed in France in July 1918, the group was assigned to the 1st Pursuit Wing and saw action in the final months of the war, supporting the Battle of Saint-Mihiel and the Meuse-Argonne Offensive.",
